        "text": "Variable scope in Java code blocks",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "A variable declared inside a code block is scoped to that block and cannot be accessed outside of it, resulting in a compilation error if referenced elsewhere.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Declaration location for variables in Java",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Variables can only be declared inside code blocks (enclosed by curly braces). Declaring a variable outside a block causes a compilation error.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    },
    {
      "topic": {
        "text": "Simplifying boolean assignment",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_text": {
        "text": "Instead of using an if‑else statement to set a boolean based on a condition, you can assign the result of the boolean expression directly to the variable; the expression evaluates to true or false automatically.",
        "refs": ["Q0003", "Q0004"]
      },
      "explanation_type": null
    }
  ],
  "examples": [],
  "facts": [
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Variables must be declared inside a code block (curly braces) in Java.",
        "refs": ["Q0000"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "A variable declared inside a code block is only available within that block.",
        "refs": ["Q0001"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Giving a boolean variable an initial value (e.g., false) allows later assignment without needing an else clause.",
        "refs": ["Q0002"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    },
    {
      "fact_text": {
        "text": "Wrapping a boolean expression in parentheses improves readability but is not required for correctness.",
        "refs": ["Q0004"]
      },
      "fact_type": null
    }
  ],
